.TH CATALIST 1 "November 2026" "v@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
catalist \- local-first anime and manga tracker for the terminal
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B catalist
.br
.B catalist import
\fIFILE.xml\fR...
.br
.B catalist export
\fIanime\fR|\fImanga\fR
.br
.B catalist
\fB--help\fR | \fB--version\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B catalist
tracks the anime you watch and the manga you read in two CSV files on your
computer. Run without arguments, it opens the terminal interface. It asks
Jikan, the public MyAnimeList API, to look up a title to add, to refresh a
title's episode or chapter count after it changes (and once a day for the
titles being watched or read) and to fetch covers, which it draws with
sixel graphics through img2sixel.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR import " " \fIFILE.xml\fR...
Add the titles of MyAnimeList XML exports. A title already in the catalogue
keeps its score, progress and dates. All files are read before
anything is added, so a bad file changes nothing.
.TP
.BR export " " \fIanime\fR | \fImanga\fR
Print that list as MyAnimeList XML, which the import pages of MyAnimeList
and AniList read. Titles without a MyAnimeList id are left out and counted
on standard error.
.TP
.BR -h ", " --help
Print usage and the data directory.
.TP
.BR -v ", " --version
Print the version.
.SH TABS
.TP
.B 1 Anime, 2 Manga
Left, the filters by status and by rating from 10 to 0 with their counts,
and a stats card (days spent, mean score, episodes or chapters, rewatches,
volumes for manga, a bar of the statuses); in the middle, the sortable list
with a New column of released episodes or chapters not yet seen; right, the
cover, then the details and tracking cards.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1 2 Tab
Switch tab.
.TP
.B j k g G h l
Move, jump, and change pane.
.TP
.B + - P S R
Progress, next status, one star more.
.TP
.B e Enter
Open the details card. There, \fBj\fR and \fBk\fR pick a field (status,
rating, progress, total, volumes for manga, rewatches), \fBh\fR and \fBl\fR
change it by one, and \fBe\fR or \fBEnter\fR types a number.
.TP
.B n u c t s r p
Sort by new releases (the default), last updated, date, title, status,
rating or progress; again to reverse.
.TP
.B / a d
Filter by title, add a title, delete (asks first).
.TP
.B q
Quit. Changes are saved as they are made.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/catalist/anime.csv, manga.csv
The catalogue.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CATALIST_DATA_DIR
Use this directory instead of ~/.config/catalist.
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
When set, the catalogue is kept in $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/catalist.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 when the work failed (a file could not be read or saved),
2 when the command line is wrong.
.SH AUTHORS
McKaigne <https://github.com/McKaigne/Catalist>
